//? Title: Coordinate-based imitation policy
//? Lang: en

> Coordinate-based imitation policy

The shared grid policy uses normalized row and column coordinates,
a tanh hidden layer and four action logits. A training batch contains
coordinate rows and expert action IDs. Each update minimizes mean
negative log-likelihood and retains Adam state for the next batch.
The same policy can fit a fixed demonstration set or take new
labels collected during a rollout.

This small fit learns the change in expert action at the bottom row.
The plot compares the probability of moving right before and after
training down a single column. The [behavior cloning report|behavior_cloning.mepml]
evaluates complete rollouts after fitting a larger demonstration set.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/grid_imitation.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

int main() {
  namespace n=dm::nn;
  std::vector<float> positions;
  std::vector<double> rows(7);
  std::iota(rows.begin(),rows.end(),0.);
  for (int row=0;row<7;++row) positions.insert(positions.end(),{float(row)/6,.5f});
  const auto features=n::from_vector(positions,{7,2});
  const auto actions=n::from_vector<int>({1,1,1,1,1,1,3});
  dm::rl::ImitationPolicy policy(2,16,4);
  const auto before=policy.predict(features);
  for (int step=0;step<150;++step) policy.train(features,actions);
  const auto after=policy.predict(features);
  const double start=n::sparse_softmax_cross_entropy(before,actions).item();
  const double finish=n::sparse_softmax_cross_entropy(after,actions).item();
  if (!(finish<start)) throw std::runtime_error("Imitation loss did not improve");
  std::print("Action NLL decreased from {:.6f} to {:.6f}.\n",start,finish);
  const auto right=[](const auto& logits) {
    return n::slice(n::softmax(logits,-1),{0,3},{7,1}).template to_vector<double>();
  };
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.lines(rows,right(before),"Before fitting",{217,96,26})
      .lines(rows,right(after),"After fitting",{37,99,235})
      .title("Fitting a directional expert").x_label("Grid row").y_label("Probability of moving right")
      .ylim(0,1).size(800,460).save_svg("build/grid_imitation.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Action NLL decreased from 1.431187 to 0.064020.
